## Production Integrity Tests (Hard Gate -- Non-Deferrable)

Every story that modifies or introduces anything that affects the deployed
product must include production integrity tests **in the same commit**. These
are a hard gate equivalent to code review and QA -- they cannot be carried
over, marked as follow-up, or excused during gate validation. If the tests
don't exist, the story fails QA automatically. No exceptions.

**1. Data integrity.** For any computed value: a live smoke test that fetches
the API response, independently recomputes the expected value from the raw
inputs available in the same response, and asserts they match. No mocking.
Real endpoint, real data, real math.

**2. API-to-UI fidelity.** For any value displayed on screen that originates
from the API: a test that fetches the same API endpoint, reads the rendered
value from the DOM, and verifies the displayed value matches the API value
with correct formatting.

**3. Visual consistency.** For any CSS or layout change: a test that verifies
computed styles match the design system values.

**4. Cross-layer contract.** For any new or modified API field: verify the
full path from computation -> API response -> UI render -> DOM assertion.
The test must exercise the complete chain, not isolated layers.

**5. Bundle verification.** After every UI deploy: fetch the deployed
assets and verify the changed selectors/properties are present in the output.
This catches duplicate selectors, build caching, and deploy failures.

**Evidence required:** Log all production integrity test file paths and
pass/fail output in the story file under "Production Integrity Tests".
Gate validation check #6 will reject stories missing this section. QA
will reject stories missing any of the 5 checks. Code review will
classify missing production integrity tests as Critical.

