## API, Schemas, and Test Fixtures

- When an epic includes both API-producing and API-consuming stories, the epic
  spec must include an explicit response schema example for each endpoint.
- Stories that change an API response shape must audit all test fixtures
  referencing that endpoint and update them to match the new shape in the same
  commit.
- Test fixtures that mock API response shapes must match the response schema
  documented in the architecture addendum. Fixture/schema mismatches are
  Important severity (not Suggestion).
- Tests that validate data against the same system that produced it (circular
  self-validation) must be flagged as a test gap during code review. A
  validation test that can never fail is not a test.

