## Story Spec Quality

- Stories MUST NOT exceed 7 acceptance criteria. If a story exceeds 7 ACs,
  split it into smaller stories.
- Story ACs MUST reference behaviors or symptoms, not specific file names.
- Story specs created from carry-over backlog items or user instructions must
  include a "Source Requirements" section that quotes the original requirement
  verbatim. The story must address every root cause listed in the carry-over
  entry. This is the enforcement mechanism for Autonomy Rule 8.
- Stories that rename a field or label across layers must include ALL surfaces
  where the old name appears -- not "check and defer" but "check and fix."
- Stories that remove, rename, or convert identifiers/labels must grep ALL
  directories in the project, not a hardcoded subset.

