## Sprint Process

- The sprint-close docs commit is the last commit in the sprint.
- No informal carry-overs. Every item not resolved in the current sprint must
  be formally documented in `_bmad-output/planning-artifacts/carry-over-backlog.md`
  before the retro closes.
- No conditional deferral. Never mark a retro finding or carry-over item to be
  fixed "the next time component X is touched."
- When a code review approves a story with deferred implementations, each
  deferral must be added as a carry-over backlog item.

---

## Code Review and Validation

- Suggestion-level code review findings that are not fixed during the review
  cycle are discarded when the story closes. They are NOT added to the
  carry-over backlog. If a finding is worth tracking, it must be elevated to
  Important.
- Dead code (unreferenced constants, always-true conditionals, unused variables)
  in files modified by the current story must be classified as Important
  severity, not Suggestion.

